=Renato |year=2022 |title=Numerical Infinities and Infinitesimals in Optimization |series=Emergence, Complexity and Computation |volume=43 |publisher=Springer |location=Cham |doi=10.1007/978-3-030-93642-6 |isbn=978-3-030-93642-6 }}</ref>\n\n<ref name=\"DAlottoKvasov2026\">{{cite web |last1=D'Alotto |first1=Louis |last2=Kvasov |first2=Dmitri E. |title=What Stronger Mathematical Language Can Reveal About Computation, Sets, and Infinity |website=SIAM News |publisher=Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics |date=2026-09-21 |url=https://www.siam.org/publications/siam-news/articles/what-stronger-mathematical-language-can-reveal-about-computation-sets-and-infinity/ |access-date=2026-10-05 }}</ref>\n\n}}\n\n[[Category:Applied mathematics]]\n[[Category:Arithmetic]]\n[[Category:Foundations of mathematics]]\n[[Category:Infinity]]\n[[Category:Mathematical logic]]\n[[Category:Nonstandard analysis]]\n[[Category:Number theory]]\n[[Category:Numerical analysis]]\n[[Category:Philosophy of mathematics]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-30T06:39:37Z","lastrevid":1382450117,"length":22568}]}}